      ":question/problem": "![](images/c0/c01ec68e17d8f5946dd6c0774fe9a49d3bd8d45fd357a429bd9a418ec9f9a6fe.png)\n\nThe base of a solid is the region enclosed by the curves $y = x^{2} - x - 1$ and $y = 1 - x - x^{2}$, as shown in the picture. Given that cross-sections perpendicular to the $x$-axis are semicircles, calculate the volume of the solid.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
